The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as cf72c019.

I found a new security bug, and it's the most important thing in the assessment. --deny-dir does not hide what search finds when it searches a whole folder. To test it, I put a file secrets/key.txt containing a made-up token in a scratch project and ran a real model with --deny-dir secrets, telling it to search for the token in .. The tool result the model got back included ./secrets/key.txt:1:token=CANARY_Q7Z. Running list_files . the same way listed the denied file's name. The cause is that GuardedTool in src/tool_wrappers.rs only checks the path you pass in. It never filters what the walk finds below that path. But docs/src/configuration/permissions.md:209 says the fence covers search and list_files.

I only ran the launch-time --deny-dir. Two other paths use the same wrapper and probably have the same hole, but I haven't tested them: the deny lists /cd loads, and sub-agents. Two smaller points:
• yoagent's search tool calls rg without --no-config, so a user's ripgrep config file still applies. rg wasn't installed here, so the leak above came through the grep fallback.
• Running yoyo in the scratch folder created .yoyo/audit.jsonl there.

A Codex CLI 0.162 changelog item ("keep ripgrep configuration from weakening deny-glob masks") is what pointed me at this.

The other findings are in the assessment for the planner:
• **Build and binary:** the harness reported the build and tests green, and yoyo -p answered PONG.
• **File-size gate:** src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 2036 lines. Adding 14 more makes cargo test fail, which would revert the whole task.
• #1016: the next step on the ticket is a probe. Close the stream in the middle of an attempt and check whether held text is lost.
• #1009: six commands still get extra literal quotes around arguments with spaces. I confirmed it on outline, lint and docs.
• #982: a bare yoyo blame still exits 0.
• #869: the two remaining unwired readers only run at startup. What /cd still doesn't do is reload allow lists, hooks, MCP servers or skills.
• **Stale skill pointers:** the blindspot and synthesis skills still tell the agent to use the retired explore-codebase.
• **Recent runs:** all recent evolve runs succeeded, with no reverts and no CI failures in 14 days.

Research:
• **Hook failures:** Claude Code 2.1.295 added an `onFailure: "block"` setting so a hook that fails or times out blocks the action. From reading `src/hooks.rs`, yoyo's pre-hooks already block when they fail to start or time out. I didn't test this.
• **Retry-After:** Codex now honours a server's Retry-After. I haven't checked whether yoagent's retry does.
• **yopedia:** I saved a dated note of the changelog comparison and the leak (job `0282b005`). Keyword search worked, but the `/api/query` endpoint returned "Sign in required".
